    "content": "In a move to strengthen the agricultural sector, Kenyan President William Ruto has announced that the government will reduce the cost of maize seeds by 50 percent beginning in September 2026. The announcement was made during a public event in Taita Taveta, where Ruto detailed plans to lower the price of a maize seed bag from 300 to 150 Kenyan shillings. This initiative is part of broader efforts to encourage local farming and boost national food output.\n\nThe subsidy is not limited to seeds alone. The government also plans to cut the price of a 50-kilogram bag of fertilizer by 500 shillings, reducing its cost from 2,500 to 2,000 shillings. These measures are designed to ease the financial burden on farmers, who often struggle with high input costs, and to incentivize increased cultivation of maize, a staple crop in Kenya.\n\nThe timing of the announcement is significant, as it comes ahead of the planting season, allowing farmers to plan and budget accordingly. By making essential inputs more affordable, the government hopes to see a rise in maize production, which could help stabilize food prices and reduce reliance on imports.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom maintain close ties to their homeland and engage in cross-border trade, this policy could have ripple effects. Cheaper maize production in Kenya may lead to more affordable grain in regional markets, potentially benefiting Somali consumers and businesses. Additionally, diaspora members investing in Kenyan agriculture may find new opportunities as input costs decline.\n\nPresident Ruto emphasized that the subsidy is part of a long-term strategy to achieve food security in Kenya. While specifics on implementation and funding were not fully detailed, the government has signaled its commitment to supporting farmers through targeted interventions. Observers will be watching to see how these changes affect yields and market prices in the coming months.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/24/kenya-oo-50-dhimaysa-qiimaha-abuurka-galleyda-laga-bilaabo-sebtembar/",
